.TH "cbor::cycles_t" 3 "Version 0.9.0" "mbedded-cbor" \" -*- nroff -*-
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
cbor::cycles_t \- Selects the encode that writes each cycle of a tree with tags 28 and 29 (RFC 8949 3\&.4, IANA tags 28 and 29)\&.  

.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.PP
\fR#include <cbor/encode\&.hpp>\fP
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP 
Selects the encode that writes each cycle of a tree with tags 28 and 29 (RFC 8949 3\&.4, IANA tags 28 and 29)\&. 

\fBcbor::encode()\fP and \fBcbor::encode_iov()\fP without it write no tag 28 or 29 of their own, and a \fRshared_reference\fP gives \fRunsupported_value\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
bytes: d8 1c 82 d8 1d 00 d8 1d 00
call: auto const tree = cbor::decode(bytes)
result: owning item of 28([29(0), 29(0)])
call: std::string out;
result: ""
call: cbor::encode(**tree, out, cbor::cycles)
result: 9
call: out
result: 9 bytes: d8 1c 82 d8 1d 00 d8 1d 00
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBcbor::encode()\fP 
.RE
.PP

